  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating the Red Village concept</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Our dream: Ready for change through localised humanitarian innovation. Still too often &#x2018;solutions&#x2019; are driven by external stakeholders, offering &#x2018;their solution to our problem&#x2019;. This should not be the starting point of humanitarian innovation. Instead, our journey should start the source, and we will prove that a Red Village can be such an entry point for humanitarian innovation. Based the living lab principle, we will create the Movement&#x2019;s first permanent ecosystem that takes our partners on a journey, creating meaningful humanitarian solutions for real-life challenges faced by vulnerable people affected by crises, now and in the future.

Together with our selected partner National Societies, in partnership with TUD&#x2019;s Green Village and others, we will establish a functioning Red Village: A thriving &#x2018;living lab&#x2019; ecosystem. Key characteristics of a Red Village are: 1) A safe, controlled creative space, 2) At the heart of communities directly affected by humanitarian strife, 3) Local needs meet humanitarian innovation and research processes, and 4) Operated through a public-, private-, and people partnership. Having these characteristics in mind, solutions are co-created and eventually deployed within the humanitarian response system.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The exact location will be determined during the initial stage. Careful selection of a partner NS is part of the implementation process</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The work currently envisaged under this initiative includes 3 workstreams:
Inclusive partnership: An inclusive user-driven partnership on addressing humanitarian challenges identified by vulnerable people faced by disasters is established in a structured  and sustainable manner
Financing model: Innovative inclusion- and financing models are developed, pitched to and embraced by a network of like-minded alternative financing instruments
Physical space: The foundation for a permanent space is established in one selected country. It is the node that  connects users with service delivers, knowledge institutes, humanitarian actors and financing agencies</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There is currently not a perment space for innovation. The project tries to solve this</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">We will work with organisations that have experience in establishing living labs, for example TUD Green Village</narrative>
  </description>
